; toggle-admission-band.fk — change as the price of entry, over the evening's own sensors.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk observe/toggle-admission.fk
;
; Every fixture is witnessed on 2026-07-22, not invented: the mac ear's pitch window, the
; phone playhead sampled three times at 20:59, the phone step counter's 16:40 burst, and
; the SemaCompanion binary read at 21:29 and again at 21:44.
;
; Verdict 1023 when, on Go / Rust / TypeScript / fkwu:
;     1  the ear window holds 5 distinct pitches
;     2  so the ear is admitted and its reading passes through unchanged
;     4  the playhead holds exactly 1 distinct value across three samples
;     8  so its reading is turned away — -1, not 814
;    16  and the reason given is 1: never seen to move
;    32  the step counter HAS been seen to move
;    64  yet its reading is still turned away, five hours after the fact
;   128  and the reason given is 2: moved, but long ago — a different number, deliberately
;   256  the binary, read at two sizes an hour apart, is admitted
;   512  and that same admitted binary's 21:29 sample does not stand at 21:44 — the
;        companion half, which was prose ordering the reader around until 22:25
;
; The teaching: this settles admissibility, never correctness. The playhead's 814 may have
; been perfectly true; the point is that three identical samples cannot tell anyone whether
; it was. And the two refusals carry different reasons on purpose — a sensor that never
; moves and a sensor that stopped moving need different repairs, and collapsing them into
; one "untrusted" loses the only part that says what to do next.
;
; The sting in bit 256: the binary is admitted BECAUSE it changes, which is exactly why the
; 21:29 reading of it was worthless by 21:44. Admission is a property of the instrument and
; buys no shelf life for any sample it produced.

(do
    (toggle-admission-check))
